---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SkillsToolkit from '../components/SkillsToolkit.astro';
---

<Layout title="Experience" description="Professional experience spanning DC CAP, Common App, University of Virginia, and Teach For America. PhD, MPP, IES Fellow.">
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-16 lg:px-8 lg:py-24">
		<h1 class="text-h1 mb-6 font-semibold text-neutral-900">
			Experience
		</h1>

		<p class="text-dek mb-16 max-w-3xl font-heading text-neutral-900">
			Across classrooms, academic research, the largest college application dataset in the country, and nonprofit leadership, I've built the teams and the systems that move outcomes for students.
		</p>

		<div class="space-y-20">
			<section>
				<h2 class="text-h2 mb-12 font-semibold text-neutral-900">
					Professional Experience
				</h2>

				<div class="space-y-16 border-l-2 border-neutral-200 pl-16 sm:pl-28">
					<div class="relative">
						<div
							class="absolute -left-[11px] top-2 h-3 w-3 rounded-full border-2 border-white bg-primary"
						></div>
						<div class="pl-6">
							<h3 class="text-h3 font-semibold text-neutral-900">
								Chief Strategy and Analytics Officer | DC CAP
							</h3>
							<p class="mt-1 text-base text-neutral-600">July 2023 – Present | Washington, DC</p>

							<div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700">
								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Executive Leadership:</strong> Member of the Senior Leadership Team, reporting to the CEO and supporting DC CAP's 2050 Moonshot, the organization's goal of 80% college completion for DC students. I lead roughly six people, including the Chief Programs Officer, and I lead the financial planning and analysis function: budgeting, multi-year scenario modeling, and the path-to-stability work the board reasons from. On arrival I ran a full program evaluation and pivoted DC CAP to a regional partnership model, now Pillar 1 of the FY26–28 strategy. Across that partner portfolio, DC CAP sustains <strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">85–90%</strong> first-year retention and <strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">75–95%</strong> graduation at its established partners.
								</p>

								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Innovation + Fundraising:</strong> I launched DC CAP's Innovation Hub on a <strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">$600K</strong> KPMG AI Impact Initiative grant, the organization's largest AI investment to date. The Hub houses the AI Governance Framework and the Career Pathway Intelligence Platform (launching October 2026). I have been instrumental in more than <strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">$50M</strong> in philanthropic commitments since joining.
								</p>

								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Organizational Health:</strong> I lead five units, Student Success, University Partnerships, GEAR UP, Innovation, and Data & Technology, and I built the analytics, evaluation, and storytelling infrastructure that anchors the annual fundraising model. I authored <strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">four</strong> Standards of Practice, covering disbursement, renewal, the programmatic FAQ, and staff onboarding, so the institutional knowledge no longer lives in any one person's head. Across my time at Common App and DC CAP, <strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">three</strong> direct reports have earned promotions, one of them twice.
								</p>

								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Change Management:</strong> I lead DC CAP's digital transformation. I designed the AI Governance Framework, which now governs how staff use AI day to day, and I ran the 60-day pilot that introduced it to nine staff across three units from April to June 2026. I designed the Salesforce Operational Architecture that runs the scholar lifecycle: a renewal cycle for current scholars, a tighter application and award cycle, and a communications journey across counselors, partner universities, and scholars. The application process now runs at one person and <strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">3–5 hours</strong> a week, down from roughly ten people at 20-plus hours; coach administrative load fell from about <strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">60%</strong> of a coach's time to under 10%. <strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Two</strong> production agentic systems run in-house on a shared five-agent pattern, with audit trails on every output.
								</p>

							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="relative">
						<div
							class="absolute -left-[11px] top-2 h-3 w-3 rounded-full border-2 border-white bg-primary"
						></div>
						<div class="pl-6">
							<h3 class="text-h3 font-semibold text-neutral-900">
								Senior Manager of Research & Analytics | Common App
							</h3>
							<p class="mt-1 text-base text-neutral-600">Oct 2020 – July 2023 | Remote</p>

							<div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700">
								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Founding Team Member:</strong> Second member of the founding research function at Common App, the largest college application dataset in the United States. Defined the data environment, technical stack, research agenda, and data sharing policies.
								</p>

								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">External Relations:</strong> Primary spokesperson for data insights, representing the organization to national media (NYT, Bloomberg) and the Board of Directors.
								</p>

								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Strategic Partnerships:</strong> Negotiated and managed research collaborations and data-sharing protocols with leading universities. Resulting work was profiled at NBER, Brookings, the Association for Education Finance and Policy (AEFP), and the EdWorkingPapers Series at Brown University's Annenberg Institute. Led randomized control trials on direct admissions and text-message information campaigns.
								</p>

							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="relative">
						<div
							class="absolute -left-[11px] top-2 h-3 w-3 rounded-full border-2 border-white bg-primary"
						></div>
						<div class="pl-6">
							<h3 class="text-h3 font-semibold text-neutral-900">
								IES Predoctoral Fellow, Educational Policy Studies | University of Virginia
							</h3>
							<p class="mt-1 text-base text-neutral-600">Aug 2015 – Aug 2020 | Charlottesville, VA</p>

							<div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700">
								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">UVA–Louisiana Department of Education Partnership:</strong> Policy and accountability systems research with the Louisiana Department of Education during a multi-year statewide policy rollout (2017–2020). Worked directly with state policymakers and district leaders on accountability design.
								</p>

								<p>
									<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-900">Published Research:</strong> The partnership produced peer-reviewed publications on statewide policy implementation and program quality. A longitudinal study of early-childhood program quality improvement under Louisiana's quality rating system appeared in AERA Open and ECRQ, alongside additional accountability-policy research and a policy brief.
								</p>

							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="relative">
						<div
							class="absolute -left-[11px] top-2 h-3 w-3 rounded-full border-2 border-white bg-primary"
						></div>
						<div class="pl-6">
							<h3 class="text-h3 font-semibold text-neutral-900">
								Associate Editor | Peabody Journal of Education
							</h3>
							<p class="mt-1 text-base text-neutral-600">2013 – 2015 | Nashville, TN</p>
							<div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700">
								<p>
									Managed editorial operations, review pipelines, and production scheduling for one
									of the nation's oldest education policy journals while completing MPP coursework.
								</p>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="relative">
						<div
							class="absolute -left-[11px] top-2 h-3 w-3 rounded-full border-2 border-white bg-primary"
						></div>
						<div class="pl-6">
							<h3 class="text-h3 font-semibold text-neutral-900">
								Corps Member | Teach For America
							</h3>
							<p class="mt-1 text-base text-neutral-600">2011 – 2013 | South Louisiana</p>
							<div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700">
								<p>
									Led large achievement gains in elementary school turnaround environment (95th
									percentile value-added scores). Selected as regional winner of the Excellence in
									Teaching Award.
								</p>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="text-h2 mb-12 font-semibold text-neutral-900">
					Education
				</h2>
				<div class="space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700">
					<div class="border-l-2 border-neutral-100 pl-6">
						<strong class="block text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900"
							>PhD, Educational Policy Studies</strong
						>
						<span class="text-neutral-600">University of Virginia (IES Fellow) | 2020</span>
					</div>
					<div class="border-l-2 border-neutral-100 pl-6">
						<strong class="block text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900">MPP</strong>
						<span class="text-neutral-600">Vanderbilt University (Peabody Honors Scholar) | 2015</span>
					</div>
					<div class="border-l-2 border-neutral-100 pl-6">
						<strong class="block text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-900">BA, History</strong>
						<span class="text-neutral-600">Tulane University | 2011</span>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="text-h2 mb-12 font-semibold text-neutral-900">
					Speaking
				</h2>
				<div class="border-l-2 border-neutral-100 pl-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700">
					<p>
						In FY2026 I represented DC CAP's research and technology work at three conferences: UERU, CIO4Good, and the UVA IES Program Conference.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>
		</div>
	</div>
	<SkillsToolkit />
</Layout>
